+# Cleanup following the current upstream fixes
+
+Base: GitLab `5e6d03591731f64d589661f4f329aa28e8c71a7d`. This includes the
+source-correctness fixes and the newer operation-supply, general-career and
+gold-reserve changes. Do not apply the older standalone supply patch over it.
+
+Removed the disabled centralized-production method, its declaration and caller,
+the commented virtual declaration, and abandoned commented building valuations.
+City-local wonder eligibility and the active gold-hurry phase remain in place.
+The removed method returned before its unfinished planning body; its profiling
+entry also disappears. No object fields, virtual slots or save fields change.
+
+Load and game-start initialization now share one method, preserving profiler
+flags and call order, fresh upgrade-pair rebuilding, and runtime type lookups.
+Crusade spawning selects the existing interval once and uses one spawn call:
+4 turns below an estimated 500-turn game, then 6/8/12/14/16 at thresholds
+500/700/1000/1400/1800. City iteration and the obsolete-tech guard are preserved.
+
+## Reserve arithmetic correction
+
+The upstream tests passed, but two additional cases failed:
+
+* `goldAfterReserve(INT_MAX, 99, INT_MAX)` overflowed in `rem * percent`.
+* Gold 2,000,000,000, rate -250,000,000, runway 12 and speed 50% left
+  926,258,177 available instead of 500,000,000 because the unscaled deficit
+  was saturated before applying the percentage.
+
+The replacement computes the unscaled deficit in 64 bits and compares it with
+`ceil(gold * 100 / percent)` before the final multiplication. Below that cutoff,
+the product is less than `gold * 100`; at or above it, available gold is zero.
+Thus it evaluates the intended integer formula without overflowing even when
+the unrestricted three-factor product would exceed 64 bits. Nonpositive gold,
+nonnegative rates, and nonpositive runway/percentage retain the existing guards.
+
+## Validation
+
+Run `python3 Tools/run_regression_suite.py`. The suite includes 4,352 reserve
+cases against an independent Python integer oracle, with C++03 and fatal UBSan
+checks, and 70 Crusade boundary scenarios plus lifecycle-order checks.
+These isolated tests do not build the Windows DLL or execute the BTS host.
+The source remains on save format 6; this cleanup adds no format migration.
